  "ingredients": [
    "1 cup softened butter",
    "6 cloves garlic, minced",
    "1 (4 pound) bone-in rib-eye roast",
    "sea salt and cracked black pepper to taste"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients. Preheat the oven to 500 degrees F (260 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/JggGCvShN6WIFWxQYyTgRb3_8qM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/240522-Easy-Rib-Eye-Roast-ddmfs-step-1-046-8251b62d8bcb4282b16f9c62a8319cd9.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/240522/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Beat butter and garlic together in a small bowl until combined.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/_pqMMUcv0MIuyEVKpMI0UmUvvkM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/240522-Easy-Rib-Eye-Roast-ddmfs-step-2-049-355d096e572c4953b8d033b87cfc0db6.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/240522/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Poke several holes in rib eye with a sharp knife. Rub butter mixture all over meat and season generously with salt and pepper. Place rib eye fat-side up in a roasting pan.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/ab4nYt-4sAdHz89W_uvhC3A3QU0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/240522-Easy-Rib-Eye-Roast-ddmfs-step-4-055-ceed002662d742ef9f57a79925abcff4.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/240522/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast in the preheated oven for 20 minutes to develop a crust.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/5m_xuD0ln5R58VV62yAJqseHOY4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/240522-Easy-Rib-Eye-Roast-ddmfs-step-5-129-8e53644ace1e45da86888a7efde1e679.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/240522/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduce heat to 325 degrees F (165 degrees C) and continue cooking until rib eye is reddish-pink and juicy in the center, 1 ½ to 2 hours. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center will read 145 degrees F (63 degrees C) for medium. Let rest before slicing.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Bf1Gksh74r73ag32jXDzvqhK4lI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/240522-Easy-Rib-Eye-Roast-ddmfs-step-5-2-131-7e17952487794f25afc8f34cc012d0c3.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/240522/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/GC0gSM7D-Vq1VElat2zxUTATUzE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/240522-Easy-Rib-Eye-Roast-ddmfs-4x3-142-d28046bc42b948da977539659a74ee14.jpg"
      ],
